 "equipment_type": "Boiler",
 "applies_to": "Lochinvar SYNC 1.0 / 1.3 / 1.5 dual-module boilers and water heaters with the Modbus/BACnet communication board, per SYNC-MODB Rev L.",
 "summary": "Lochinvar's SYNC appliances have two heat modules and talk Modbus RTU through an RS-485 communication board. The BAS writes a configuration word, an enable word, a rate or setpoint command and optional remote temperatures; it reads switch and flame states, outlet/inlet/flue temperatures for both modules, cascade power and status, blocking and lockout codes.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "Addresses are printed Modicon-style (00001, 10001, 30001, 40001). Subtract the table base and 1 for the wire address; the manual's exception-code text confirms PDU addresses start at 0."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Modbus and BACnet Communication Instructions - SYNC models 1.0 - 1.3 - 1.5",
  "doc_number": "SYNC-MODB 100161723_2000017706 Rev L",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://assets.lochinvar.com/damroot/Original/10014/594260SYNC-MODB_100161723_2000017706__REV%20L_BACNET.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 3-6 (Modbus configuration, exception codes), 7-8 (memory map, configuration bits), 18-21 (unit operation, conversions), 22-23 (codes)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Temperatures: the conversion section says the unit passes temperatures in degrees C and the value must be divided by 10 (examples: 26.7 C sent as 267; outlet 683 = 68.3 C). Scale 0.1 is applied to the temperature registers with 0.1 resolution in the map.",
  "Left out: System/Cascade Setpoint (30004), Outlet Setpoint 1 and 2 (30008, 30017) and Tank Setpoint (40004). The map gives them a 0.5 C resolution while the conversion text says temperatures are C x 10, so their scaling is not settled.",
  "Left out: Firing Rate 1 and 2 (30012, 30021). The map prints a 0.1 resolution for a 0-100 % value but no example confirms whether the raw value is % or % x 10.",
  "Signed types: inlet, flue and BAS-supplied temperatures have negative minimums in the map and are listed as INT16; the manual itself only says 16-bit word.",
  "Configuration bit 7 names a System Return Temperature, but the SYNC map lists no register for it (it stops at 40007).",
  "The DHW remote-control example table labels 40004 as 'Rate Command'; the memory map has the rate command at 40003 and the tank setpoint at 40004.",
  "Input registers 30001-30003 are packed copies of the discrete inputs; the bit order is not stated, so they are UINT16. Use the discrete inputs instead."
 ],
